Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.02,0:00:16.78,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,You've completely made that your own.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.29,0:00:20.20,Default,THERON,0,0,0,,Yeah. I'm itching to use it in actual combat.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.63,0:00:23.45,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,Hey, I've got a question for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.45,0:00:25.12,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,What'd you think of the demons?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.87,0:00:32.25,Default,THERON,0,0,0,,Well... how should I put it?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.25,0:00:36.01,Default,THERON,0,0,0,,They're definitely strong, \Nbut they're not all that scary.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.43,0:00:43.33,Default,THERON,0,0,0,,When we first encountered them, \Nrumor and legend dominated my impression,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:43.33,0:00:47.27,Default,THERON,0,0,0,,but the more I learned, \Nthe less terrifying they became.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.58,0:00:50.28,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,No matter how powerful they may be,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.28,0:00:54.31,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,they ultimately aren't much different from us,\N so they're not something to fear.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:54.31,0:00:55.28,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,Is that what you mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.73,0:00:59.03,Default,THERON,0,0,0,,Yeah, that. That's exactly it.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.63,0:01:02.46,Default,THERON,0,0,0,,What is it? What's up?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.83,0:01:07.47,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,Nothing. I was just considering maybe \Nyou and I do think alike after all.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:07.47,0:01:09.94,Default,THERON,0,0,0,,Ugh, you're creeping me out.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:14.42,0:01:17.02,Main - Italics,KYLE/ID,0,0,0,,So that contributed to his decision.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:18.27,0:01:20.27,Flashback,KYLE,0,0,0,,You let the female demon go?!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.91,0:01:22.89,Flashback,THERON,0,0,0,,Y-Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:23.47,0:01:25.81,Flashback,KYLE,0,0,0,,After I explicitly told you not to?!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.81,0:01:28.15,Flashback,THERON,0,0,0,,A lot happened on our end, okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:28.53,0:01:31.67,Flashback,KYLE,0,0,0,,Damn it. I wasn't counting on this.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:31.67,0:01:35.78,Flashback,THERON,0,0,0,,I mean, she didn't seem like\N such a bad person.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:36.18,0:01:40.89,Main - Italics,KYLE/ID,0,0,0,,If she were truly a threat, \NTheron never would've let her get away.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:41.25,0:01:48.83,Main - Italics,KYLE/ID,0,0,0,,Perhaps three centuries of temporary peace \Nhas changed humanoids and demons alike.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:48.83,0:01:50.87,Default,LIESE,0,0,0,,Oh, there you are.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:52.21,0:01:54.80,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,Are you two feeling better already?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:55.17,0:01:58.62,Default,LIESE,0,0,0,,Yeah. The doctor gave us\N clean bills of health.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:58.62,0:02:00.66,Default,LIESE,0,0,0,,We could get right back in the fray!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:02.03,0:02:04.53,Default,URZA,0,0,0,,I wasn't particularly injured.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:04.53,0:02:07.81,Default,URZA,0,0,0,,I got a lot of rest, so I'm fine now.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:08.07,0:02:11.14,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,I see. You both did well.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:12.05,0:02:14.71,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,I'm so glad you both survived.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:15.49,0:02:16.41,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:18.83,0:02:22.25,Default,LIESE,0,0,0,,It was no big deal. Really.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:22.25,0:02:25.66,Default,URZA,0,0,0,,S-Seriously. Don't be so dramatic.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.79,0:02:30.00,Default,THERON,0,0,0,,Well, this is irritating to watch.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.61,0:02:38.73,Default,GOH,0,0,0,,Good day, Kyle. Dad's in the back.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:38.73,0:02:39.67,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,Thanks.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:40.94,0:02:45.06,Default,GOH,0,0,0,,Um, Sildonia, there's something\N I'd like to discuss with you.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.51,0:02:47.56,Default,SILDONIA,0,0,0,,Fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.03,0:02:55.25,Default,SILDONIA,0,0,0,,So, what do you wish to discuss?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:55.25,0:02:58.82,Default,GOH,0,0,0,,R-Right! Um, you see...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:01.55,0:03:03.26,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,Looks like you've recovered.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:05.14,0:03:09.83,Default,GAZUS,0,0,0,,In spite of the exhaustion from \Nsomeone's unreasonable request, yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:12.26,0:03:14.30,Default,GAZUS,0,0,0,,I hear you're leaving tomorrow.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:14.30,0:03:16.09,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,Yeah. That's the plan.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:17.47,0:03:20.58,Default,GAZUS,0,0,0,,I'd like to give you a parting gift.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:34.42,0:03:37.70,Default,GAZUS,0,0,0,,Sheaths for your blade \Nand the Holy Sword Rand.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:37.70,0:03:42.45,Default,GAZUS,0,0,0,,Since you gave me a ton of mithril \Nand all, I made these to practice.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:42.83,0:03:44.05,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,I appreciate it.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:44.05,0:03:47.45,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,Sildonia isn't fond of cheap sheaths.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:47.94,0:03:49.97,Default,GAZUS,0,0,0,,You've done a lot for me.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:50.35,0:03:53.89,Default,GAZUS,0,0,0,,I won't waste the mithril you provided.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:56.34,0:03:57.96,Default,GOH,0,0,0,,Sildonia...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:57.96,0:04:00.71,Default,GOH,0,0,0,,Are you really leaving?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:00.71,0:04:04.26,Default,SILDONIA,0,0,0,,Indeed. According to Kyle, we depart tomorrow.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.69,0:04:08.72,Default,GOH,0,0,0,,Um, do you think that maybe...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:08.95,0:04:12.23,Default,GOH,0,0,0,,you could stay here with me forever?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.18,0:04:18.39,Default,SILDONIA,0,0,0,,I'm afraid I cannot do that.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:18.39,0:04:21.36,Default,SILDONIA,0,0,0,,Where Kyle goes, I must follow.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:21.36,0:04:23.26,Default,GOH,0,0,0,,Oh, but please.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:23.26,0:04:27.12,Default,GOH,0,0,0,,I'd love for you to teach me more things.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.27,0:04:29.51,Default,SILDONIA,0,0,0,,Goh...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:31.05,0:04:34.69,Default,SILDONIA,0,0,0,,Never fear. I have taught you\N all you need to know.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:34.69,0:04:39.89,Default,SILDONIA,0,0,0,,With Kyle's patronage, you will be able\N to complete the golem on your own.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:42.33,0:04:45.42,Default,GOH,0,0,0,,I see. So you can't stay, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:45.42,0:04:47.66,Default,SILDONIA,0,0,0,,Do not take it personally.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:47.66,0:04:50.74,Default,SILDONIA,0,0,0,,At present, I belong to Kyle.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.31,0:04:52.14,Default,SILDONIA,0,0,0,,What is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:52.14,0:04:54.66,Default,GOH,0,0,0,,Er, it's nothing...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:55.34,0:04:56.69,Default,GOH,0,0,0,,I understand.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:56.69,0:04:59.02,Default,GOH,0,0,0,,I'll let it go. All of it.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.02,0:04:59.82,Default,SILDONIA,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.82,0:05:03.90,Default,SILDONIA,0,0,0,,I'm not sure what you mean, \Nbut you have potential.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:03.90,0:05:06.13,Default,SILDONIA,0,0,0,,Keep devoting yourself to your craft.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:08.01,0:05:10.31,Default,GOH,0,0,0,,Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:12.74,0:05:15.99,Default,SILDONIA,0,0,0,,Ah, Kyle! Have you concluded\Nyour business already?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:15.99,0:05:16.85,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:17.47,0:05:20.55,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,I'm counting on you \Nto complete the golem, Goh.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:21.70,0:05:22.92,Default,GOH,0,0,0,,Okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:23.23,0:05:24.59,Default,SILDONIA,0,0,0,,Take care.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:26.78,0:05:29.91,Default,GOH,0,0,0,,Kyle already has Liese and Urza...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:30.31,0:05:32.18,Default,GOH,0,0,0,,Must he take Sildonia too?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:32.82,0:05:37.19,Main - Italics,SILDONIA/NA,0,0,0,,Kyle would come to be known by many names.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:37.42,0:05:43.14,Main - Italics,SILDONIA/NA,0,0,0,,They say the "lecherous hero" \Nmoniker originated here in Karan.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:54.97,0:06:00.58,Main - Italics,KYLE/NA,0,0,0,,I learned from Miranda that \NGovernor Bax had passed.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:04.67,0:06:08.05,Flashback,BAX,0,0,0,,Glory to Karan...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:12.13,0:06:13.23,Flashback,GAZUS,0,0,0,,Governor!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:17.29,0:06:19.51,Main - Italics,KYLE/NA,0,0,0,,He didn't have long to begin with,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:19.94,0:06:25.05,Main - Italics,KYLE/NA,0,0,0,,but upon finding out that all he'd done\Nwas for naught, he took a turn for the worse.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:27.02,0:06:33.70,Default,MIRANDA,0,0,0,,Governor Bax confessed the whole truth \Nregarding the kidnappings on his deathbed.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:33.70,0:06:35.79,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,Then this ordeal is...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:35.79,0:06:40.62,Default,MIRANDA,0,0,0,,Yes. We may consider it resolved,\Nalthough one problem remains.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:41.06,0:06:45.25,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,The massacre at the Gargan embassy, you mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:45.25,0:06:46.34,Default,MIRANDA,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:46.34,0:06:52.14,Default,MIRANDA,0,0,0,,The empire will blame Zirgus for the \Nincident and put the squeeze on us.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:52.93,0:06:58.29,Default,MIRANDA,0,0,0,,Since Queen Milena has called off her \Nengagement, who knows what they'll demand?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:58.62,0:07:00.22,Default,MIRANDA,0,0,0,,My head hurts.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:00.90,0:07:04.75,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,I have no choice but to leave \Nthe matter in your hands.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:05.53,0:07:06.71,Default,MIRANDA,0,0,0,,Yes, I know.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:07.11,0:07:10.06,Default,MIRANDA,0,0,0,,Forgive me for complaining.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:10.06,0:07:12.16,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,Don't worry about it.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:12.51,0:07:17.41,Default,MIRANDA,0,0,0,,Also, Gazus has now officially\Nbeen selected as the next governor.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:17.86,0:07:22.79,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,Really? But he's cooped up in his workshop.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:22.79,0:07:23.91,Default,MIRANDA,0,0,0,,That's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:24.30,0:07:26.42,Default,MIRANDA,0,0,0,,He accepted the role on the condition
Dialogue: 0,0:07:26.42,0:07:32.13,Default,MIRANDA,0,0,0,,that we handle the work while he spends \Nas much time blacksmithing as he desires.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:34.98,0:07:37.24,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,So that's the story, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:37.24,0:07:40.69,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,He already made us sheaths for our swords.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:40.69,0:07:42.64,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,He said he was practicing with mithril.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:44.46,0:07:46.43,Default,MIRANDA,0,0,0,,That sounds just like him.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:46.43,0:07:48.83,Default,MIRANDA,0,0,0,,Saying they were practice was only an excuse.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:48.83,0:07:53.71,Default,MIRANDA,0,0,0,,If not for you, there would have\N been far more casualties.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.21,0:07:58.54,Default,MIRANDA,0,0,0,,Both Gazus and I thank you \Nfrom the bottom of our hearts.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:01.83,0:08:05.02,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,Could I ask a personal question?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:05.02,0:08:06.57,Default,MIRANDA,0,0,0,,Yes, of course.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:07.66,0:08:10.62,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,Goh had some money trouble recently.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:11.34,0:08:14.05,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,You were pulling the strings\N behind that, weren't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:14.05,0:08:15.01,Default,MIRANDA,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:15.69,0:08:22.74,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,Threatened by Governor Bax, Gazus distanced \Nhimself from you to keep you out of things.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:23.39,0:08:30.39,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,Unaware of the situation, you came up with a \Nplan to force the two of you closer together.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:30.83,0:08:34.58,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,You set your sights on Goh, \Nwho was looking for investors.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:35.31,0:08:37.91,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,You didn't even act as an intermediary.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:37.91,0:08:42.62,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,You just suggested to the right people \Nthat there was a business opportunity.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:43.27,0:08:50.05,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,Then you waited for it to blow up, intending\N to earn Gazus's favor by rescuing Goh.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:50.90,0:08:53.53,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,Even if I'm wrong, I doubt I'm far off the mark.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:54.34,0:08:57.82,Default,MIRANDA,0,0,0,,I'm in awe. Your deductive\N skills are impressive.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:58.61,0:09:02.72,Default,MIRANDA,0,0,0,,However, do you have any concrete proof?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:03.21,0:09:05.48,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,Unfortunately, no.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:05.48,0:09:07.94,Default,MIRANDA,0,0,0,,Well, that's a shame.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:07.94,0:09:12.36,Default,MIRANDA,0,0,0,,In that case, isn't this all mere conjecture?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:12.71,0:09:14.43,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,It would seem so.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:14.43,0:09:16.99,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,Why don't we both forget I said it?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:17.36,0:09:21.33,Default,MIRANDA,0,0,0,,Say what you will, but that was\N a rather serious accusation.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:21.33,0:09:24.37,Default,MIRANDA,0,0,0,,However did you manage to come to it?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:24.78,0:09:31.38,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,Well, you see, I know you have no qualms \Nabout doing something so calculating.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:31.62,0:09:32.42,Default,MIRANDA,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:34.79,0:09:38.89,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,If you've got something to feel guilty about,\NI'd like you to do me a favor.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:39.39,0:09:45.78,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,Could you make sure no one learns the details \Nabout Goh's golem restoration project?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:46.39,0:09:50.01,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,No nation can know. Not even Zirgus.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:50.73,0:09:54.78,Default,MIRANDA,0,0,0,,If that's all you require, \NI believe I can do that.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:56.31,0:09:58.10,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,Then we have a deal.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:59.11,0:10:03.89,Default,MIRANDA,0,0,0,,But do you really believe he'll succeed?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:04.33,0:10:07.97,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,Who invests in a project they expect to fail?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:10.09,0:10:11.83,Default,MIRANDA,0,0,0,,I suppose you have a point.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:12.27,0:10:16.05,Default,MIRANDA,0,0,0,,But this golem would be\N a major boon to our forces.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:16.05,0:10:19.95,Default,MIRANDA,0,0,0,,If all goes well, I will have\N to report it to the kingdom.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:20.65,0:10:24.06,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,Well, I don't expect you to hide it forever.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:24.70,0:10:28.22,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,Just avoid attracting attention \Nuntil his research is on track
Dialogue: 0,0:10:28.22,0:10:30.81,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,and implementation is in sight.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:30.81,0:10:31.90,Default,MIRANDA,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:33.39,0:10:34.54,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,It's all right.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:34.95,0:10:37.67,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,Even if it takes a while,\Nit won't be more than three years.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:37.67,0:10:40.20,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,There'll be no need\Nto keep it secret after that.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:41.26,0:10:42.70,Default,MIRANDA,0,0,0,,Um...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:42.70,0:10:44.93,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,Don't make that face.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:44.93,0:10:49.23,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,I'd rather see you smiling instead.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:49.81,0:10:53.46,Default,MIRANDA,0,0,0,,I'm amazed you can say that\N after threatening me.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:56.62,0:10:58.37,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,You're absolutely right.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:59.30,0:11:06.47,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,But you look much better now \Nthan when you were just surviving.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:06.82,0:11:07.87,Default,MIRANDA,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:08.79,0:11:16.48,Default,MIRANDA,0,0,0,,Forgive the odd question, \Nbut have we met before?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:17.97,0:11:21.61,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,No. We met for the first time here in Karan.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:48.07,0:11:49.77,Default,THERON,0,0,0,,Aw, man.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:50.05,0:11:53.60,Default,THERON,0,0,0,,I never got to properly test my sword.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:53.60,0:11:55.05,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,Don't say that.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:55.05,0:11:56.79,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,You'll get the chance soon enough.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:57.13,0:12:01.00,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,For now, we should return \Nto Zirgus and make our report.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:01.00,0:12:05.66,Default,SILDONIA,0,0,0,,Perhaps I'll have them treat me\N to another snack or two.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:06.70,0:12:08.45,Default,THERON,0,0,0,,That's all you think about.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:08.45,0:12:11.29,Main - Top,SILDONIA,0,0,0,,What do you mean, that's {\i1}all{\i0}?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:08.77,0:12:12.75,Default,LIESE,0,0,0,,They'll probably ask us all kinds \Nof questions about our trip.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:11.29,0:12:14.05,Main - Top,KYLE,0,0,0,,Now, now. She needs the nutrients.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:13.18,0:12:16.92,Default,URZA,0,0,0,,Yes, there will be no avoiding that.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:14.05,0:12:16.62,Main - Top,SILDONIA,0,0,0,,I'll turn you into a snack and eat you!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:16.62,0:12:17.29,Main - Top,THERON,0,0,0,,What?!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:17.29,0:12:23.59,Default,URZA,0,0,0,,There were already tensions between \NZirgus and the Gargan Empire over Karan.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:24.59,0:12:30.22,Default,URZA,0,0,0,,Who knows how much the assassination of\Na key figure will impact their relationship?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:32.34,0:12:34.79,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,We know the demons are up to something.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:35.29,0:12:36.86,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,We have bigger problems.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:38.25,0:12:40.51,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,They could be planning an attack.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:40.95,0:12:43.49,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,If we're busy fighting amongst ourselves,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:43.49,0:12:45.70,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,that could spell the worst possible outcome.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:46.27,0:12:50.79,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,That's why we're working to unite humanoids.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:51.38,0:12:53.25,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,We can change our fate.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:56.95,0:12:58.21,Default,THERON,0,0,0,,Damn, dude.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:58.59,0:13:01.65,Default,THERON,0,0,0,,You're always so motivated.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:12.55,0:13:15.58,Default,MILENA,0,0,0,,This is a difficult situation.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:16.97,0:13:18.25,Default,AUGES,0,0,0,,We've been informed that
Dialogue: 0,0:13:18.25,0:13:22.73,Default,AUGES,0,0,0,,all three princes were urgently summoned \Nto the imperial capital of Ruos.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:23.23,0:13:27.83,Default,AUGES,0,0,0,,At this rate, tensions between \Nour two nations will only worsen.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:27.83,0:13:29.74,Default,MILENA,0,0,0,,Yes, I know.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:30.78,0:13:32.62,Default,MILENA,0,0,0,,Auges, Kilren.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:33.14,0:13:35.18,Default,MILENA,0,0,0,,I have a mission for you two.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:42.21,0:13:43.10,Default,CERAIA,0,0,0,,There.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:48.15,0:13:51.25,Default,CERAIA,0,0,0,,I wonder if Kyle's doing okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:57.42,0:14:00.54,Default,LAYLA,0,0,0,,You're as helpless as ever\Nwith everything that's not magic.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:01.37,0:14:03.30,Default,CERAIA,0,0,0,,Layla! Good morning.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:03.30,0:14:06.40,Default,LAYLA,0,0,0,,Hey, Ceraia. Working hard, I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:06.40,0:14:08.14,Default,CERAIA,0,0,0,,You're leaving already?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:08.14,0:14:12.41,Default,LAYLA,0,0,0,,Yeah. If I see them, I'll say hello for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:12.41,0:14:16.41,Default,CERAIA,0,0,0,,Anything can happen on the road. Be careful.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:16.70,0:14:20.42,Default,LAYLA,0,0,0,,Sure. This is a critical time for you too.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:20.42,0:14:22.09,Default,LAYLA,0,0,0,,Don't strain yourself.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:32.43,0:14:34.27,Default,LIESE,0,0,0,,Hey, look!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:41.27,0:14:42.44,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,That's...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:50.35,0:14:51.70,Default,THERON,0,0,0,,There. I'm all out.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:51.70,0:14:52.82,Default,URZA,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:54.62,0:14:58.73,Default,THERON,0,0,0,,Traveling by carriage is nice \Nand easy, but it's a bit boring.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:00.55,0:15:02.15,Default,LIESE,0,0,0,,My turn next.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:03.41,0:15:04.91,Default,URZA,0,0,0,,I won't lose this time.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:05.75,0:15:07.46,Default,LIESE,0,0,0,,We'll see about that.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:11.15,0:15:14.07,Default,LIESE,0,0,0,,Maybe I'll take this one.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:15.74,0:15:17.89,Default,LIESE,0,0,0,,Or maybe this one.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:19.98,0:15:21.10,Default,LIESE,0,0,0,,This one!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:21.10,0:15:22.74,Default,LIESE,0,0,0,,I'm all out too!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:22.74,0:15:25.11,Default,URZA,0,0,0,,H-How did you know?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:25.11,0:15:28.49,Default,LIESE,0,0,0,,It was written all over your face. \NI read you like a book.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:28.97,0:15:30.61,Default,URZA,0,0,0,,O-One more game.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:31.13,0:15:34.86,Main - Top,LIESE,0,0,0,,Sure, but I might win again.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:31.54,0:15:34.27,Default,THERON,0,0,0,,It takes five days to get there.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:34.27,0:15:35.98,Default,THERON,0,0,0,,Let's take it easy.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:34.86,0:15:36.37,Main - Top,URZA,0,0,0,,I'll win this time.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:37.46,0:15:43.79,Default,KILREN,0,0,0,,I am grateful you would accept\N such a sudden request, Sir Kyle.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:44.27,0:15:46.59,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,No, I'm honored to.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:47.01,0:15:50.64,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,"Demons were entirely \Nresponsible for the tragedy
Dialogue: 0,0:15:50.64,0:15:56.10,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,at the imperial embassy in Karan,\N which was not a hostile act by Zirgus."
Dialogue: 0,0:15:56.10,0:16:00.13,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,As the man who cut down one of their number, \NI can personally attest to that.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:00.13,0:16:03.10,Default,KILREN,0,0,0,,We sincerely appreciate your testimony.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:03.59,0:16:10.08,Default,KILREN,0,0,0,,The success of this conference and the peace \Nbetween our nations rests on your shoulders.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:10.08,0:16:12.49,Main - Italics,KYLE/ID,0,0,0,,She's really putting on the pressure.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:13.11,0:16:16.87,Default,AUGES,0,0,0,,Now, now. You needn't get so worked up.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:17.14,0:16:26.14,Default,AUGES,0,0,0,,Worst case, war breaks out, and either Zirgus\N or the Gargan Empire will be destroyed.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:26.14,0:16:30.26,Default,KILREN,0,0,0,,Minister Auges, do not joke about grave \Nmatters concerning our nations.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:30.26,0:16:34.72,Default,AUGES,0,0,0,,Forgive me. I simply think\N we oughtn't be so uptight.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:34.72,0:16:40.06,Default,AUGES,0,0,0,,You're nervous because you've never borne \Nsuch a great responsibility, aren't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:40.52,0:16:44.33,Default,AUGES,0,0,0,,As for me, I am accustomed \Nto visits to the empire.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:44.33,0:16:46.96,Default,AUGES,0,0,0,,Let me handle everything.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:46.96,0:16:48.33,Default,KILREN,0,0,0,,Well, well.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:48.33,0:16:53.42,Default,KILREN,0,0,0,,Climbing from a low-ranking official to \Nminister with the backing of King Remonas
Dialogue: 0,0:16:53.42,0:16:55.67,Default,KILREN,0,0,0,,sure changes the way a man speaks, hmm?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:59.78,0:17:01.61,Default,AUGES,0,0,0,,I wouldn't say that.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:02.25,0:17:03.94,Default,KILREN,0,0,0,,Don't be so modest.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:05.11,0:17:06.54,Default,AUGES,0,0,0,,No, really.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:07.57,0:17:08.80,Default,KILREN,0,0,0,,Oh, please.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:08.80,0:17:10.53,Main - Top,AUGES,0,0,0,,No, if {\i1}you{\i0} please!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:10.53,0:17:12.01,Main - Top,KILREN,0,0,0,,No, if {\i1}you{\i0} please!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:10.77,0:17:12.79,Main - Italics,KYLE/ID,0,0,0,,Please let us get there soon.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:12.01,0:17:13.14,Main - Top,AUGES,0,0,0,,No, if {\i1}you{\i0} please!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:13.14,0:17:14.05,Main - Top,KILREN,0,0,0,,If {\i1}you{\i0} please!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:19.05,0:17:21.10,Default,LIESE,0,0,0,,Oh, you can see the city now!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:21.10,0:17:25.44,Default,URZA,0,0,0,,This is my first time visiting Ruos. \NI had no idea it was so huge.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:25.44,0:17:31.07,Default,THERON,0,0,0,,Let's really let 'em treat us\Nat tonight's dinner party.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:31.90,0:17:34.07,Main - Italics,KYLE/ID,0,0,0,,The Gargan Empire, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:34.85,0:17:36.15,Main - Italics,KYLE/ID,0,0,0,,I might get to see {\i0}him{\i1}.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:48.94,0:17:55.72,Default,ELDRAND,0,0,0,,Zirgus insists that they were also victims\Nof the massacre at the embassy.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:55.72,0:17:58.43,Default,CONRAD,0,0,0,,They claim it was all the work of demons.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:58.43,0:18:01.05,Default,CONRAD,0,0,0,,Do they really expect us to believe that?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:01.05,0:18:05.18,Default,CONRAD,0,0,0,,Demons haven't appeared\N in the last three hundred years!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:05.57,0:18:12.21,Default,ELDRAND,0,0,0,,Yet according to Zirgus's report, \Nsomeone slew the demon responsible.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:13.18,0:18:16.39,Default,ELDRAND,0,0,0,,Alzard was among the victims.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:16.70,0:18:21.07,Default,ELDRAND,0,0,0,,If that's true, it would make this supposed\N champion one of humanity's strongest.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:21.07,0:18:23.60,Default,CONRAD,0,0,0,,It's inconceivable that anyone
Dialogue: 0,0:18:23.60,0:18:28.09,Default,CONRAD,0,0,0,,could be stronger than our wyvern knights\N and second most powerful court sorcerer.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:28.82,0:18:32.34,Default,CONRAD,0,0,0,,I will not entertain Zirgus's lies any longer.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:32.70,0:18:35.57,Default,CONRAD,0,0,0,,And you, Maiser! What's with the attitude?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:35.57,0:18:39.01,Default,CONRAD,0,0,0,,The Gargan Empire's authority \Nis being threatened!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:41.01,0:18:44.58,Default,MAISER,0,0,0,,You're both a bit too tense, don't you think?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:45.18,0:18:47.85,Default,MAISER,0,0,0,,I hear there's a hero in Zirgus.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:48.17,0:18:50.87,Default,MAISER,0,0,0,,Perhaps he's the one who defeated the demon.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:53.07,0:18:54.79,Default,ELDRAND,0,0,0,,What makes you say that?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:54.79,0:18:56.13,Default,MAISER,0,0,0,,Just a hunch.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:57.62,0:18:58.86,Default,ELDRAND,0,0,0,,A hunch, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:59.74,0:19:03.69,Default,ELDRAND,0,0,0,,Your hunches are often correct, Maiser.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:28.87,0:20:30.90,Default,MAISER,0,0,0,,You sure work quick.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:31.79,0:20:32.73,Default,MAISER,0,0,0,,Am I interrupting?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:33.14,0:20:36.06,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,No, we weren't discussing anything important.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:37.11,0:20:40.42,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,Anyway, do you have business with me?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:40.42,0:20:43.82,Default,MAISER,0,0,0,,Yeah. I prefer to be direct.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:44.65,0:20:46.43,Default,MAISER,0,0,0,,Let me cut to the chase.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:46.85,0:20:49.26,Default,MAISER,0,0,0,,Will you serve me?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:50.35,0:20:53.19,Default,KYLE,0,0,0,,I'm glad you'd think so highly of me, but—
Dialogue: 0,0:20:53.19,0:20:57.69,Default,MAISER,0,0,0,,If you won't, I believe I should\N eliminate you here and now.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:58.79,0:21:01.17,Default,MAISER,0,0,0,,You're too capable.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:01.65,0:21:04.82,Default,MAISER,0,0,0,,If you won't be my ally, \Nthen I can't have you around at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:06.13,0:21:09.55,Default,MAISER,0,0,0,,What do you say, Kyle Leonard?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:26.88,0:22:31.18,Default,CREDITS,0,0,0,,{\fnTimes New Roman\an3\blur.5\shad0\fs8\bord1\c&H000000&\3c&HC6C4C8&\pos(578.769,251.846)}Translation:\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h{\fs11}Sho Stifler\N\N{\fs8}Timing:\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h{\fs11}Andy Ellis\N\N{\fs8}Editing:\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h{\fs11}Riley Dalton{\fs12}\N\N{\fs8}Quality Check:\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h{\fs11}William Haggard\N\N{\fs8}Translation Check:\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h{\fs11}Elizabeth Ellis
Dialogue: 0,0:22:56.62,0:22:58.10,Default,YULIGA,0,0,0,,Forgive me.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:58.83,0:23:03.77,Default,YULIGA,0,0,0,,Though we found the holy sword during our \Ninvestigation, we failed to acquire it.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:04.97,0:23:07.51,Default,YULIGA,0,0,0,,It also seems Garnias has perished.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:11.99,0:23:17.79,Default,YULIGA,0,0,0,,I will gladly accept any punishment\Nto make up for this failure.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:21.06,0:23:22.65,Default,YULIGA,0,0,0,,What is your command...
Dialogue: 0,0:23:24.43,0:23:26.26,Default,YULIGA,0,0,0,,Demon King Ruiza?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:34.97,0:23:40.25,Default,SIGN,0,0,0,,{\an8\fnArial Black\shad0\blur1\3c&HB2A56D&\pos(320,213)}Thank you for watching!
